==================================================================
  slowclient.sh 
==================================================================
ceiling = 2, two readers at 32KB/s, then one normal request
timeouts.downstream_write = 30s

  response                     status   latency   capacity returned?
  buffered 1MiB                200      163ms     yes
  buffered 4MiB                503      3120ms    no
  buffered 16MiB               503      3020ms    no
  streaming (chunked)          503      3154ms    no

Rows above are diagnostic: whether a given size stalls depends on the
socket buffers between origin and client, which are not portable.

Asserted: with timeouts.downstream_write = 2s, the stall is bounded

  response                     status   latency   capacity returned?
  streaming, bounded write     200      105ms     yes

parameters: os=Linux, arch=x86_64, cpus=6, rustc=1.98.0, profile=debug, commit=a48b30a, downstream_write=30s, bounded_downstream_write=2s, ceiling=2, reader_rate=32k

PASS: slow readers can delay observed origin end-of-stream, but timeouts.downstream_write bounds it: capacity was back within 105ms of the deadline

