==================================================================
  forwarded.sh 
==================================================================
forwarded headers, with the peer untrusted and then trusted

  untrusted X-Forwarded-For is replaced            origin saw 127.0.0.1
  untrusted X-Forwarded-Proto is replaced          origin saw http
  client-supplied Forwarded is stripped            origin saw nothing
  a spoofed scheme cannot split the cache key      1 render
  7 invented schemes, one URL                      1 render
  forged host/port/prefix/identity are restated    host=127.0.0.1:20776 port=20776
  a forged host cannot poison a shared page        1 render, canonical unchanged
  malformed and non-ASCII values are survivable    ok
  Host-less HTTP/1.0 forwards no invented host     HTTP/1.1 200 OK
  trusted X-Forwarded-For is believed              origin saw 203.0.113.7
  trusted X-Forwarded-Proto is believed            origin saw https
  the walk stops at the rightmost untrusted hop    origin saw 203.0.113.7
  an invented scheme is refused even when trusted  origin saw http
  trusted http and https are separate entries      2 renders
  trusted public host and TLS scheme are preserved https://shop.example:443
  a spoofed prefix cannot choose host or scheme    shop.example
  believed public hosts are separate cache entries 2 renders
  untrusted IPv6 peer                              ::1 / [::1]:27337
  trusted IPv6 proxy chain                         2001:db8::7
  source: none reads nothing, even from a trusted peer 127.0.0.1 / http

parameters: os=Linux, arch=x86_64, cpus=6, rustc=1.98.0, profile=debug, commit=a48b30a, render_ms=100

PASS: forwarded metadata is a claim, and Tanod treats it as one: an untrusted client can move neither the origin's view of it nor the cache key, a trusted proxy is believed, the hop walk resolves to the address a trusted proxy observed, and no unkeyed header can poison a shared response

